# CPack-style packaging notes
# Current project version: 0.1.0 for Project Tahoe X86
#
# This is a packaging metadata note and assembly reference, not generated output.
#
# Current packaging target name: tahoe-shell
# Expected artifact location after build: build/bin/tahoe-shell
#
# Packaging must preserve:
# - The exact application name used by the shell CMake target
# - The version string used by the project
# - The separation between verified and planned behavior
#
# Packaging rules:
# - Do not generate installers or packages until the build is verified.
# - Do not embed secrets, OAuth tokens, or user-specific config.
# - Do not claim a package is bootable or installable until it has been built and tested.
#
# Linux packaging notes:
# - A CPack-driven package may be appropriate once the shell builds.
# - Desktop entry, icons, and file associations belong in a separate install manifest.
#
# Cross-platform installer notes:
# - Optional installer prep may exist for other platforms, but it must be labeled as such.
